## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-account data pipelines with lineage, schema evolution, and data quality gates in AWS.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account data access
- Parquet data format and partitioning
- Schema evolution with Glue
- Data lineage and quality gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: gate for schema drift
function checkSchema(record, expected) {
  if (record.schemaVersion !== expected) {
    throw new Error('Schema drift detected');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle late-arriving data in daily partitions?
- What monitoring would you implement for data quality failures?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests diagnosing streaming governance, tenant isolation, schema evolution, and automated remediation in real-time.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant schemas, Glue Schema Registry, data masking, Lake Formation permissions
- Parquet partitioning, Glue Catalog, lineage via EventBridge, testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: mask email/phone in streaming records before land
function maskPII(record) {
  if (!record) return record;
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.user) {
    if (r.user.email) r.user.email = '***@***.com';
    if (r.user.phone) r.user.phone = '******';
  }
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift across tenants? 
- What metrics would you emit for data quality?
